                    by Goodpaster.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d387-f2" n="2" xml:id="d387-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d388"><hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d387-f3" n="3" xml:id="d387-f3-content">
                <p>Not attached to the source text. For text, see U.S. Congress, Senate, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Report of the Committee on Foreign Relations on
                        Executive L, Eighty-First Congress, First Session, The North Atlantic
                        Treaty</hi> (Washington, 1949), p. 23.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d387-f4" n="4" xml:id="d387-f4-content">
                <p>Dulles left Washington by air for Dallas
                    at 11:59 a.m., October 27, and returned at 4:15 p.m., October 28. (Dulles’ Appointment Book; Princeton University
                    Library, Dulles Papers) For text of his address before the Dallas Council on
                    World Affairs, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>,
                    November 5, 1956, pp. 695–699.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
